  "notes": "Two parallel contributing failure modes feed the SG level oscillation: the rapid-downpower/turbine-trip sequence stemming from the steam leak, and a separate SGWLC operating-methodology/barrier inadequacy described independently in the cause narrative. Both LEADS_TO the oscillation node per rule 5's parallel-trigger guidance; only the chain's origin (fm_crack) carries the CAUSED_BY edge to the official cause code X per rule 5, since the leak/crack is the narrative's stated 'direct cause' and the code is 'Other' (not independently derivable to Personnel Error for the SGWLC barrier issue). Condenser Steam Dump and AFW are described as having performed successfully during the event (not merely design context) so were modeled as INVOLVES systems rather than backups, since no explicit BACKED_UP_BY language ('remained operable throughout', 'was available') was used for a specific inoperable primary system — this event is a reactor trip/actuation, not an ECCS inoperability, so BACKED_UP_BY edges were not applicable to this consequence."
